{
  "note": "jit-verify: [MonoJit] (docs/527 §3, ts3native 0.36.173, counters v911, asi game-copy/ts3native.asi.mono1106e, list of 27 methods / 58 bodies, docs/537 §8) correctness in game: every listed method runs compiled, one call in 16 per method runs a second time in EA's interpreter from the restored state, and every live word must match. Correctness only, no timing. Direct=0: compiled-to-compiled frames do not exist in this build. [MonoFast] CallPath stays at the ini's 0, so these jobs use EA's call path. Pass per job: no crash, 0 watchdog lines, ScriptError count as the job's baseline, jitOn 2, jitMethods >= the compilable count of the list (read the 'jit: ... refused' lines: a generic body refused for its hash is a finding, not a pass), jitVerified > 100000, jitMismatch 0 (any mismatch: the method is off for the session and named in 'jit verify MISMATCH' lines, which logForbid fails on every job with no allow entry: a load-time mismatch lands before the /native before snapshot, so a jitMismatch delta rule misses it; triage before anything else), jitFaults 0. On a mismatch in a C5 row rerun with [MonoJit] Groups=255 (bit 256 holds initobj, isinst, shr.un.i8, the float moves and the direct internal calls). Read jitLarge, jitAbandoned, jitOtherTid as coverage. The log says when GC_malloc_atomic was left alone ([MonoThread] GcLock). The last job runs the same verify under [AutShadow] Mode R (docs/527 §4.4). Run: node tools/harness/queue.ts tools/harness/queues/jit-verify.json --no-smoke Direct rounds (docs/537, ts3native 0.36.173, counters v911, asi game-copy/ts3native.asi.mono1106e): the *-jit-lazy-chain jobs add [MonoJit] Direct=1 DirectLeaf=0 (chains, guarded callvirt; DirectLeaf=1 has one listed edge in docs/data/jit-call-edges.csv, docs/537 §8), still Mode=2: pass 1 takes the lazy calls, pass 2 is EA interpreter only, so a mismatch is a lazy-frame bug. Run them after jit-reader-trap.json; a job here also needs jitLazyMats > 0 (frames were written) and jitLazyFrames >= jitLazyMats.",
